source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
List what is published and why, or choose what to publish.

Usage: ink select [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Examples
  # List every page, whether it is published, and why
  ink select

  # Publish one page of a vault
  ink select notes/trip.md

Arguments
  [PATHS]...  Pages to select, as paths in the folder:
              `publish: true` is written into the
              frontmatter of each, which the file must
              already have. Without a path or `--folder`,
              every page is listed with whether it is
              published and why

Options
      --folder <GLOB>  Select every file a glob matches
                       (`notes/**`) by adding it to
                       `include` in ink.toml
      --remove         Take the selection back: remove
                       `publish: true` from each page, or
                       the glob from `include`. In a public
                       source a page that is not selected is
                       still published by default
      --dry-run        Say what would be written and write
                       nothing

Exit codes
  0  Done; warnings, if any, were printed
  1  The site has errors
  2  Wrong usage, or a folder that is missing; nothing was
     changed

See also  ink explain, ink pin
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log,
          --log-file (see `ink --help`)
